version: 2.0.0
description: Platform-specific HTTP routes for agent-driven UI, overview aggregation, git management, and ambient coordination
components:
  AgentCommandRoute:
    description: POST /api/platform/agent-command — receives navigate/highlight/annotate/observe/clear commands, broadcasts via WS
    type: route
    tags: [feature, agent-ui]
  OverviewHandler:
    description: GET /api/platform/overview — aggregates project info, symbol counts, lore stats, calibration, tasks, health metrics, and recent activity
    type: route
    tags: [feature, dashboard]
  GitRouter:
    description: /api/git/* — 8 endpoints for git status, branches, log, diff, stage, unstage, commit, push
    type: router
    tags: [feature, git]
  DocsRouter:
    description: /api/docs/* — 6 endpoints for manifest, symbol pages, flow pages, portal, custom pages, and search
    type: router
    tags: [feature, docs]
  AmbientRouter:
    description: /api/ambient/* — 5 endpoints for event stream queries, nomination management, SSE real-time streaming, and data policy
    type: router
    tags: [feature, ambient]
    signals: ["!ambient:event", "!ambient:nomination"]
  TasksRouter:
    description: /api/tasks/* — read-only HTTP over the v7 claimant task DAG (list w/ status/priority/tag/claimant filters, /board captain run-DAG, /inbox per-claimant, /calibration archetype×taskType grid, /:id). / and /board attach a computed estimate{min,max,n,source} + taskType per task (the learned-calibration story-point). Owns no storage; mutation stays on the write router.
    type: router
    tags: [feature, tasks, calibration]
  TasksWriteRouter:
    description: /api/tasks/* WRITE verbs — POST /:id/{claim,start,done,block,unblock} each PROXY the enforced updateTask state machine (no bypass), plus POST /sync (inbound two-way GitHub reconcile through the same writers). Verbs fire a best-effort outbound GitHub projection; a done settle broadcasts a live agent:annotate. portal.yaml ^write-capable.
    type: router
    tags: [feature, tasks, task-sync, enforcement]
  WarplineRouter:
    description: /api/warpline/* — READ-ONLY HTTP over the @a-company/warpline engine (the Convergence/Divergence Oracle), imported in-process (never shells the CLI). GET /ledger (reads .warpline/oracle.jsonl, version-guarded on schemaVersion, newest-first), GET /refs (local branches + HEAD), POST /forecast (ephemeral meaning forecast, no ledger write), POST /oracle (full Oracle, appends ledger), POST /diff (semantic diff), GET /absorb/:ref (serialized WarpState). An in-process concurrency semaphore (cap 2) guards every absorb-spawning handler; a per-ref WarpState cache reuses deterministic absorbs. fs.watch the ledger → !oracle-record-appended over the WS bus. NO git-write/weave path (HEAD/index/worktree untouched), but POST /oracle APPENDS to .warpline/oracle.jsonl — a state mutation declared in portal.yaml as ^write-capable while the reads + ephemeral computes are ^read-only. User refs pass an allowlist validator (REF_RE) and the engine interposes --end-of-options (git-exec) so a leading-dash ref can't be an arg-injection. FABRIC-NATIVE CONSOLE LANE (PHASE 1 re-point, native-first) — five GET-only fabric views, DAEMON-BACKED when warplined serves this fabric — GET /fabric/status (tip + transport mode + daemon status), GET /fabric/refs (native refs/heads + head pickIds), GET /fabric/shadow-tail?n=, GET /fabric/knot/:selector (SELECTOR_RE allowlisted; 404 when none), GET /fabric/grade-report?window=. Transport swap, not a redesign — when .warpline/daemon.sock exists AND the human has minted the read-SCOPED console token (`warpline daemon token mint console --kind human --scope read`, auto-discovered via consoleReadToken which structurally never returns a full-power row), responses ride DaemonClient and are the engine shapes VERBATIM (G3), byte-identical to the in-process fallback (tests/platform-warpline-router.test.ts); no daemon / no token / transport failure falls back in-process (zero breakage; a DaemonRpcError NOT_FOUND is authoritative → 404). Read-only stays LAW at three layers — GET-only route registrations, the read-scoped token, and the daemon's server-side READ_ONLY_VERBS ceiling.
    type: router
    tags: [feature, warpline, oracle, append-only-ledger, native-first, daemon]
    signals: ["!oracle-record-appended"]
  AcademyRouter:
    description: /api/academy/* — READ-ONLY HTTP over @a-company/university-core (7.11.0, replaces the deleted /api/university router that read JSON course files). GET /packs (discoverPacks + an implicit project pack when .paradigm/university has content but no pack.yaml; per-type counts, sections, skillCount), /packs/:packId/paths, /paths/:id (steps resolved to note/quiz titles), /notes/:id ({frontmatter, body}), /quizzes/:id (WITH answers — the client grades), /skills (#skill-loader listPackSkills; trust always external, never script bodies or dirs), /search?q=&type=&pack=. :packId must match a discovered pack (404); ids must match ^[A-Za-z0-9-]+$ (400); bodies load by id through the core loader with the discovered packRoot — input is never path-joined; no absolute paths leave the server. Engine imports are lazy; a throw becomes 500 { error }. portal.yaml ^local-only + ^read-only. GET /search rejects q longer than 200 characters with 400.
    type: router
    tags: [feature, university, academy, read-only]
  MemoryRouter:
    description: "/api/memory/* — READ-ONLY HTTP over the Memory Steward engines (Phase C1, TD-2026-09-20-669). GET /review calls buildDigest DIRECTLY (never reviewCommand, which writes remediations + a review stamp) → returns the advisory hygiene digest verbatim { root, scanned, pinned, items: DigestItem[] }. GET /sync?projection=true|false calls computeSync (PURE — the only mutator writeSyncResult is not reachable here) + unifiedDiff → returns the lean-rewrite PREVIEW { root, memoryFile, existed, changed, bytesBefore/After, linesBefore/After, demoted[], deduped[], projectionEnabled, projectionItems[], diff } — the full before/after bodies are intentionally WITHHELD (only the diff string). Owns no storage; NO write endpoints (apply/write verbs arrive in C2/C3). Every handler is fail-open — an engine throw becomes 500 { error }, never crashes the server. portal.yaml ^local-only + ^read-only."
    type: router
    tags: [feature, memory, read-only]
  MemoryWriteRouter:
    description: /api/memory/* WRITE verbs (Phase C2/C3, TD-2026-09-20-669) — POST /:id/prune, /:id/route { to }, /merge { ids[] }, /:id/pin each PROXY the SAME return-shaped appliers the CLI wrappers call (applyPrune/applyRoute/applyMerge/applyPin from commands/memory), so ALL path-safety (isInsideMemoryDir), archive-not-delete, and fail-open discipline live in ONE place — a browser POST is just another caller of the enforced core. Validation mirrors tasks-write (bad id → 404; bad route target or merge < 2 ids → 400; other applier failure → 409). POST /sync/write { projection? } is the GATED lean-rewrite apply — computeSync then, only when existed && changed, writeSyncResult (backup-then-atomic on MEMORY.md; original left byte-for-byte intact on any error) → { wrote:true, backupPath, bytesAfter } else { wrote:false }. On a successful mutation best-effort broadcasts memory:changed so an open ledger refreshes live. Owns no storage of its own. portal.yaml ^local-only + ^write-capable.
    type: router
    tags: [feature, memory, write, enforcement]
    signals: ["!memory:changed"]
  ClassroomRouter:
    description: "/api/classroom/* — READ-ONLY HTTP over the Academy (Classroom) gated-learning artifacts (TD-2026-06-19-007). GET /status (bootstrapped flag = curriculum dir has ≥1 *.syllabus; per-agent syllabi w/ status + certified/provisional counts; cert rollup w/ the HONEST repeatFailureRate = overturned/(survived+overturned), null when 0 resolved), GET /staged (the REAL staged candidates = study-hall JOURNAL entries from the ENROLLED agents only — those with a syllabus — read from each agent's GLOBAL journal ~/.paradigm/agents/<agent>/journal/*.yaml, one item per entry {agent, insight, confidence, trust, source, ts} newest-first; EXCLUDES entries already promoted to the notebook (promoted_to_notebook set) — once an entry graduates it is no longer a staged candidate (T-007); deliberately does NOT read the legacy Ambient nominations firehose — the Academy is the GATED-truth counterpart to Ambient), GET /certifications (cert rows from classroom-certifications.jsonl, each with a derived loop:'gated'|'legacy' from certifiedBy — gate→legacy, peer|quorum→gated, newest-first), GET /refinements (field-failure rows, newest-first), GET /rapsheet (per-certified-entry learning lineage joining the three loop spines — born=cert.ts ⋈ applied=notebook-refs.jsonl by entryId ⋈ broke=field-failures by entryId; each row {entryId, agent, concepts, certifiedBy, loop, outcome, bornTs, appliedCount, lastAppliedAt, breaks[]}; `breaks: []` means UNTESTED, never \"passed\"; sorted overturned→applied-pending→never-applied), GET /locker (Agent Locker — per-agent notebook vetting scoped to the PROJECT roster = enrolled agents ∪ agents with a project notebook, NOT the whole installed library; each agent's entries read from GLOBAL ~/.paradigm/notebooks/<agent> overlaid with PROJECT .paradigm/notebooks/<agent> deduped by id project-wins; per entry {id, title, source, trust, scope, confidence, appliedCount, brokeCount, publishable, vetted}; trust defaults to 'provisional' when unset so legacy auto-promoted entries read as BACKLOG not VETTED; vetted = trust 'certified'; sorted most-applied-first). Owns no storage; NO write endpoints. Every loader degrades to []/empty rollup on missing/malformed files (never throws on cold start). portal.yaml ^read-only."
    type: router
    tags: [feature, classroom, academy, read-only]
  BrainRouter:
    description: "/api/brain/* READ surface for the Platform Brain section (7.14.0). Every handler goes through the single #brain-view choke point openBrainView(rootHash, 'owner') — never the index or brain.yaml directly. GET /overview (brains list; badge from egressSummary — nothingLeft/count/bytes/last; recent egress rows as counts only; map = counts by type / size band / recency band over VISIBLE files; locked zones as {folder, gate, count} only — never filenames; banner = tamper copy when brain.yaml changed outside Paradigm, else null; paused = suggestions auto-paused; sets the HttpOnly SameSite=Strict brain_owner cookie — the owner token is never in a body), GET /health (computeHealth over the owner view → brokenLinks / looseNotes / sameName as plain {id,title,path} rows; links into hidden files are never 'broken'), GET /suggestions (paused flag + nextSuggestions — next ≤10 folder-first with a plain rationale string; also logs the batch to suggestions.jsonl like the CLI), GET /find?q= (view.search over title/heading/path/topic; q > 200 chars → 400; repeated q → 400; the query is NOT echoed back — reflection surface). ?brain=<rootHash> optional (invalid → 400, unknown → 404, default first brain). brainLocalGuard requires a loopback Host, an Origin (when present) EXACTLY equal to the Platform's own origin (Host port == socket port; other localhost ports refused), and Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin|none when present, on EVERY request including GETs; corsMiddleware sets ACAO on /api/brain only for the own origin. portal.yaml ^local-only + ^read-only + ^brain-default-deny."
    type: router
    tags: [feature, brain, platform, read-only, security]
    gates: ["^local-only", "^brain-default-deny"]
  BrainWriteRouter:
    description: "/api/brain/verdict WRITE (7.14.0) — POST { suggestionId, verdict: accept|reject|skip, brain? } proxies the SAME recordVerdict the CLI `paradigm brain confirm` calls (accept → declared.yaml backup + atomic write; stale → 409; unknown id → 404). ^brain-owner-write: requires the brain_owner cookie equal (timing-safe) to the per-process owner token AND an Origin exactly equal to the Platform's own origin — otherwise 403 before the body is validated. Also exports brainLocalGuard + isSameOriginBrainRequest + setBrainOwnerCookie + pickBrain + getBrainOwnerToken shared with BrainRouter. Best-effort broadcasts brain:changed. portal.yaml ^local-only + ^write-capable + ^brain-owner-write + ^brain-default-deny."
    type: router
    tags: [feature, brain, platform, write, security]
    gates: ["^local-only", "^brain-owner-write", "^brain-default-deny"]
    signals: ["!brain:changed"]
